A host runs many conversations in one process, each with credentials of
its own, and holds none itself. pi reads a configured key and its
provider and model headers, checks a provider is set up before a prompt,
and lists available models through an auth context that defaults to the
process's environment, and ModelRuntime offers no way to give it
another. A hosted conversation therefore found no key, or would have
found the host's.

Let ModelRuntime.create take an auth context and hand it to the models
and providers it builds, and mark the build so a host can refuse one
without it. Resolve a configured key or header variable only when the
context holds it, as the check before a prompt already does, since pi's
resolver otherwise falls back to the process for any variable it misses.
The synchronous fallback for an unconfigured provider can't read a
context, so a runtime given one refuses every header variable there.
Without a context, pi reads the process as before, though a value of
only spaces now counts as unset, as pi's own check already counts it.

Offered upstream as the model auth-context host seam. Apply only to the
host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays unchanged.

